  "question": {
    "text": "If the set of all values of a, for which the equation $5 x^3-15 x-a=0$ has three distinct real roots, is the interval $(\\alpha, \\beta)$, then $\\beta-2 \\alpha$ is equal to ______",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "30",
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & 5 x^3-15 x-a=0 \\\\ & f(x)=5 x^3-15 x \\\\ & f(x)=15 x^2-15=15(x-1)(x+1)\\end{aligned}$\n\n\n\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/pUMvZVXXHIIlKQkmLbX2z8xh-4Y6nyyBgItkUqjQ6EY.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\n\n\n\n$\\mathrm{a} \\in(-10,10)$\n$\\alpha=-10, \\beta=10$\n$\\beta-2 \\alpha=10+20=30$",
    "image": null
  },
